:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"7c7e38f3-2c78-5b87-9a78-4823ef519ba4\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\\n\\nSelect all that apply.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\cos x$.\\n\\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\\\pi.$” is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}+n\\\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\\n\\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\\\pi.$” is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\\n\\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=2n\\\\pi.$” is false. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\\\pi+2n\\\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included.\"} {:db/id 17592186512037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"8bff8249-7504-555f-be44-93509f6404dc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512045} {:answer/id #uuid \"f00d828f-4cec-58a5-91f7-1bdc5581b061\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"8bff8249-7504-555f-be44-93509f6404dc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512045} :answer-field/id #uuid \"46af296d-ac52-5707-8c33-19b0485010c5\" :answer-field/key \"The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"a577b525-33d1-59d7-9d08-2416b782fa30\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512055} {:answer/id #uuid \"eee8f946-7af8-57cd-9343-31374d050e1f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a577b525-33d1-59d7-9d08-2416b782fa30\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512055} :answer-field/id #uuid \"bdef17a1-0ca6-5de6-9b2f-4f6d1c7c7635\" :answer-field/key \"The function is zero at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1073a385-2025-5e44-85c8-a77883dab9dc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186511986} {:answer/id #uuid \"f2fd0bf8-c0af-5423-b210-aeb376e469ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1073a385-2025-5e44-85c8-a77883dab9dc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186511986} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c709ddee-abbd-58d2-b360-b51bad5c2ed0\" :answer-field/key \"The function has a minimum value at $x=\\\\pi.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512063}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"7d66d22a-1573-536f-81a3-9bbc4d9fa1b3\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\\\cos x$?\\n\\nSelect all that apply.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\cos x$.\\n\\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement “The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$” is true. At $x=0$, the function has value $\\\\cos 0=1$.\\n\\n- Statement “The function is zero at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}.$” is true. $\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}\\\\right)=0$.\\n\\n- Statement “The function has a minimum value at $x=\\\\pi.$” is true. $\\\\cos(\\\\pi)=-1$.\"} {:db/id 17592186512050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"4b192095-5672-5232-b8ab-2c0548a96342\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512013} {:answer/id #uuid \"ba29e56b-fef3-5a57-a9e8-d0c4add12d83\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ba29e56b-fef3-5a57-a9e8-d0c4add12d83\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512060} :answer-field/id #uuid \"14b0533b-39e8-506f-844a-a02894500982\" :answer-field/key \"The function is zero at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186511989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"08721482-23ad-5ed6-8049-e71c416374ac\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186511984} {:answer/id #uuid \"7f9d896e-cc4b-53a8-896b-c9b7f64d70f6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"7f9d896e-cc4b-53a8-896b-c9b7f64d70f6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512038} :answer-field/id #uuid \"643b1193-cdd9-52d2-8e9a-27faaecc343e\" :answer-field/key \"The function has a maximum value at $x=\\\\pi.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512021} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3f3c66d2-4aba-59b1-b038-e2bd3d98629a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512006} {:answer/id #uuid \"73811327-d375-5451-9859-089394344445\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"73811327-d375-5451-9859-089394344445\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512029} :answer-field/id #uuid \"70e39eec-1736-52e6-a9cf-1e67949f29ef\" :answer-field/key \"The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512027}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"9caf2c13-1814-5238-bf8a-a715684afcf7\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\\\cos x$?\\n\\nSelect all that apply.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\cos x$.\\n\\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement “The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$” is true. At $x=0$, the function has value $\\\\cos 0=1$.\\n\\n- Statement “The function is zero at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}.$” is true. $\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}\\\\right)=0$.\\n\\n- Statement “The function has a maximum value at $x=\\\\pi.$” is false. $\\\\cos(\\\\pi)=-1$.\"} {:db/id 17592186512069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"42868a5d-2294-5aba-8bc3-3903089d47fd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512009} {:answer/id #uuid \"c8669141-affc-5f16-aba9-f7dd4716a792\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"c8669141-affc-5f16-aba9-f7dd4716a792\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512064} :answer-field/id #uuid \"32048f4b-d6e3-557a-b273-69b36821429d\" :answer-field/key \"The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=\\\\pi+2n\\\\pi.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"67e05fc1-6f27-5a55-b0b8-2454bb824ea2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512022} {:answer/id #uuid \"b7d3bbf8-afc9-50d1-a551-cec7b4370f7a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"67e05fc1-6f27-5a55-b0b8-2454bb824ea2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512022} :answer-field/id #uuid \"8a1d64d3-cc73-5c25-8f75-374c7c718c4a\" :answer-field/key \"The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\\\pi.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3aa5caf5-667a-5d0e-b3dd-09947d8deafd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"true\" :db/id 17592186512002} {:answer/id #uuid \"4464d916-5dd5-58e9-a4d3-34f78b7e2336\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4464d916-5dd5-58e9-a4d3-34f78b7e2336\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"false\" :db/id 17592186512011} :answer-field/id #uuid \"9f7f8471-d306-5267-a916-084d0ff2554f\" :answer-field/key \"The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\\\pi.$\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186512051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"e62133c8-9957-522b-ac43-c73e3353a608\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\\n\\nSelect all that apply.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\cos x$.\\n\\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\\\pi.$” is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}+n\\\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\\n\\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\\\pi.$” is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\\n\\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=\\\\pi+2n\\\\pi.$” is true. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\\\pi+2n\\\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included.\"} {:db/id 17592186580892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"66ee4154-2c82-5f7c-a453-639a3c26e78e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"III only\" :db/id 17592186580557} {:answer/id #uuid \"a4446db1-6811-56cb-83ad-f4290b765162\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II and III only\" :db/id 17592186580661} {:answer/id #uuid \"dc264dd9-aead-5752-b49e-de8c3a93172a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I and III only\" :db/id 17592186580731} {:answer/id #uuid \"e0766b7f-1b11-54db-a463-de8434f00db9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II only\" :db/id 17592186580738} {:answer/id #uuid \"ee1767e8-6b16-5f29-a9f2-9d13c262d7a4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I only\" :db/id 17592186580762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"dc264dd9-aead-5752-b49e-de8c3a93172a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I and III only\" :db/id 17592186580731} :answer-field/id #uuid \"bfdb6ef3-805b-5c90-be75-327e320d6c71\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186580858}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"24945ccb-291e-5b02-a82c-6983ca8e2098\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-27019\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements are true?\\n\\nI. $\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=\\\\pm \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2},\\\\pm \\\\frac{3\\\\pi }{2},....\\n$$\\n\\nII. $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ has a minimum value at $x=\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{2}$, which is equal to $-1.$\\n\\nIII. The range of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\\n\\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement I is true. The zeros of the function $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ occur at $\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}+n\\\\pi$ for any integer $n.$\\n\\n- Statement II is false. $x=\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function.\\n\\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$\"} {:db/id 17592186580899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0dd1d219-b857-5b5f-a779-302045da7712\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I and III only\" :db/id 17592186580408} {:answer/id #uuid \"3ffe0c79-47de-5b14-88c0-6da61308e7b2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II only\" :db/id 17592186580494} {:answer/id #uuid \"a2a27c37-36e7-5f80-87f2-d34f3be666ae\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II and III only\" :db/id 17592186580660} {:answer/id #uuid \"b8c7ebfd-c5dc-51d3-95b8-c30068e3aa83\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"III only\" :db/id 17592186580684} {:answer/id #uuid \"c39b7953-b317-5f0e-8c8a-8e4d700894fd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I and II only\" :db/id 17592186580693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a2a27c37-36e7-5f80-87f2-d34f3be666ae\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II and III only\" :db/id 17592186580660} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f73fd2d0-ce67-564f-8d0c-066bb7ff774e\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186580877}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"3cfbb3ff-1787-5500-ba6b-0a0c378c7517\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-103227\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$ \\n\\nI. The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=2\\\\pi$\\n\\nII. Its minimum value is $-1$\\n\\nIII. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\\n\\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement I is false since $\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\\\pi =1\\\\ne 0.$\\n\\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the minimum value of the function is $-1.$\\n\\n- Statement III is true. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$\"} {:db/id 17592186580956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"2153b638-5a48-5879-a797-f45755fef1c8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II only\" :db/id 17592186580438} {:answer/id #uuid \"415f1c04-3325-5c6c-9e37-199d76af8270\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II and III only\" :db/id 17592186580496} {:answer/id #uuid \"9d4862ee-2fd3-59d7-a815-add17575e836\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"III only\" :db/id 17592186580652} {:answer/id #uuid \"c795e8ee-d9cc-5b4e-9318-6c3d73a0a57c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I and II only\" :db/id 17592186580698} {:answer/id #uuid \"ccbf85bc-ebfa-5124-998d-be2debcef7d7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I and III only\" :db/id 17592186580708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2153b638-5a48-5879-a797-f45755fef1c8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II only\" :db/id 17592186580438} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c1ed5084-2ed3-5f3c-8c8a-972f5c48d95c\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186580859}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"e9a2e847-6e9d-5334-8d47-3c2e8d9dab70\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-103219\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\\n\\nI. The function reaches its minimum value at $x=2n\\\\pi$\\n\\nII. The zeros of the function are $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}+n\\\\pi .$\\n\\nIII. The range of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,0].$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\\n\\n![](images/04/04f13f2dec860874174f51990f4260615e7be893a6be5f86b3b13857c4e8953f.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement I is false. The function reaches its minimum value at $x=\\\\pi \\\\pm 2\\\\pi ,\\\\pi \\\\pm 4\\\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=\\\\pi +2n\\\\pi .$\\n\\n- Statement II is true. The zeros occur at $$\\n\\\\displaystyle x=\\\\pm \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2},\\\\pm \\\\frac{3\\\\pi }{2},…,\\n$$ which can be written as $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}+n\\\\pi .$\\n\\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$\"} {:db/id 17592186581724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"234fbd64-3e71-5154-ba26-c33ca9ec6950\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\pi\" :db/id 17592186581076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"234fbd64-3e71-5154-ba26-c33ca9ec6950\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\pi\" :db/id 17592186581076} :answer-field/id #uuid \"32061a8c-5090-50ce-ba79-da5f40f5cbb1\" :answer-field/key \"field-5\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186581529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"f3aeab3b-a5ca-5a04-bcdb-bed224c74207\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186581481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"f3aeab3b-a5ca-5a04-bcdb-bed224c74207\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186581481} :answer-field/id #uuid \"727182ea-b0dc-5650-931f-1144963d2573\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186581561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"eb6337cc-bf42-5a29-9bf5-2dc359f58d8e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186581467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"eb6337cc-bf42-5a29-9bf5-2dc359f58d8e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186581467} :answer-field/id #uuid \"9a9965c6-ca41-50a9-81f8-b456e5eca1c7\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186581581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"9315993c-5171-5b3f-94b3-42d7c3c23737\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186581287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"9315993c-5171-5b3f-94b3-42d7c3c23737\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186581287} :answer-field/id #uuid \"a2515abb-3b8d-5ba1-84a6-8154a443be88\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186581585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"4afb0a0e-82c0-5586-856c-f6410ae81b8f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186581156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4afb0a0e-82c0-5586-856c-f6410ae81b8f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186581156} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d76c56e7-b4cc-5cbe-a907-4b7404595cc6\" :answer-field/key \"field-4\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186581611}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"bac76f4a-4116-5fca-a94a-36ce5cbe8b54\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-167583\" :question/problem \"Complete the following facts about the function $y=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\\n\\nThe domain of the function is $x\\\\in ($\\n{{field-1}}\\n$,$\\n{{field-2}}\\n$).$\\n\\nThe range of the function is $[$\\n{{field-3}}\\n$,$\\n{{field-4}}\\n$].$\\n\\nThe period of the function is\\n{{field-5}}.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\\n\\n![](images/96/96bd60d23237f836b77a26c5c0461a5c2a474554f0a14266b53fc5e7d999f1b7.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\\\infty ,\\\\infty ).$\\n\\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\\n\\n* The period of $\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is $2\\\\pi .$\"} {:db/id 17592186585738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"7ab5cdca-189e-52b2-be54-a0503ca79375\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186585397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"7ab5cdca-189e-52b2-be54-a0503ca79375\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186585397} :answer-field/id #uuid \"26ba861f-b15d-52e9-8a84-3a7d609f4655\" :answer-field/key \"field-3\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186585609} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"417289e7-c73a-5143-86c0-e7e05ba57000\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186585299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"417289e7-c73a-5143-86c0-e7e05ba57000\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186585299} :answer-field/id #uuid \"35efb24a-9e94-5377-b7da-2b0ab09e50f5\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186585616} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"2a7dc364-5a72-58cf-815e-4e86750bd04e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186585260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2a7dc364-5a72-58cf-815e-4e86750bd04e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\infty\" :db/id 17592186585260} :answer-field/id #uuid \"55aa2ba0-d01d-5f53-89a6-8e83b2a3c1c6\" :answer-field/key \"field-2\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186585632} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"af9c512a-03d5-54ac-b2a9-8c61ffa45614\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\pi\" :db/id 17592186585482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"af9c512a-03d5-54ac-b2a9-8c61ffa45614\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\pi\" :db/id 17592186585482} :answer-field/id #uuid \"6407632e-5356-5c51-949f-e505f5602aa1\" :answer-field/key \"field-5\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186585638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"2a5cb174-5766-5bd4-93bd-41748015067f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186585259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2a5cb174-5766-5bd4-93bd-41748015067f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186585259} :answer-field/id #uuid \"80bbfc2a-a5e7-5f5d-a854-bfe10f2ea1cd\" :answer-field/key \"field-4\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186585644}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"2b74a3d3-c29e-513b-a913-e51860e5cc88\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-167613\" :question/problem \"Complete the following facts about the function $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\\n\\nThe domain of the function is $x\\\\in ($\\n{{field-1}}\\n$,$\\n{{field-2}}\\n$).$\\n\\nThe range of the function is $[$\\n{{field-3}}\\n$,$\\n{{field-4}}\\n$].$\\n\\nThe period of the function is\\n{{field-5}}.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \\n\\n![](images/ce/cebd0527c2b8b3bcdf2948da0771103f17412ff058d74b96db1287a7046ba3bc.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\\\infty ,\\\\infty ).$\\n\\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\\n\\n* The period of $\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $2\\\\pi .$\"} {:db/id 17592186619728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"213a4c1d-b52e-5221-8ad6-bafab66ca787\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I only\" :db/id 17592186619213} {:answer/id #uuid \"34f2c4fa-9589-5f3b-a92d-7ab1dfecb4ff\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"III only\" :db/id 17592186619254} {:answer/id #uuid \"5e47ffcf-8937-546e-86c3-086790f1ca96\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II and III only\" :db/id 17592186619313} {:answer/id #uuid \"6ef1a6af-af24-5d21-9979-34303223d001\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II only\" :db/id 17592186619343} {:answer/id #uuid \"b02b9187-1038-564f-a7c8-07dfab96ffd2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"I and III only\" :db/id 17592186619453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"5e47ffcf-8937-546e-86c3-086790f1ca96\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value \"II and III only\" :db/id 17592186619313} :answer-field/id #uuid \"48d39eb1-5500-5131-a5b1-8eba2c1dc701\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186619626}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"28614a2a-126b-5809-92bc-8cfc91edc708\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-27012\" :question/problem \"Which of the following statements regarding the graph of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are true?\\n\\nI. The graph intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\\\pi .$\\n\\nII. $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ has a minimum value at $x=\\\\pi$, which is equal to $-1.$\\n\\nIII. The range of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let's plot the graph of $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\\n\\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\\n\\nLet's go through each statement.\\n\\n- Statement I is false. As $\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\\\pi )=-1$, $y=\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ does not intersect the $x$-axis at $x=\\\\pi .$\\n\\n- Statement II is true. The function has a minimum at $x=\\\\pi$ and the value of the minimum is $-1.$\\n\\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1]$\"}] :knowledge-point/title \"Describing Properties of the Cosine Function\"}",
  "records": []
}
